libphonenumber-js 1.13.11
https://github.com/catamphetamine/libphonenumber-js

The file beside this is the project's own browser build, `bundle/libphonenumber-min.js`,
taken from the published package and renamed. Nothing about it has been edited.

The library is MIT (see LICENSE). The number rules it carries are generated from Google's
libphonenumber, which is Apache-2.0:
https://github.com/google/libphonenumber

Those rules change -- countries add prefixes, ranges open, a trunk prefix stops meaning what
it meant. Update this file with a release rather than silently, and record the version here.
